.TH io_isnonblock 3
.SH NAME
io_isnonblock \- query non-blocking mode
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <io.h>

int \fBio_isnonblock\fP(int64 fd);
.SH DESCRIPTION
io_isnonblock returns whether descriptor fd is currently in non-blocking
mode: 1 if non-blocking, 0 if blocking, or -1 if fd is not a tracked
descriptor (never passed to io_fd(), io_nonblock(), or io_block()).

This reflects the last mode set through io_nonblock()/io_block() (and the
mode detected when fd was registered via io_fd()), not a live kernel
query: on native Windows, Winsock's ioctlsocket(FIONBIO) has no documented
way to read a socket's current blocking mode back from the OS, so the
result is a cache maintained by this library. If fd's mode was changed by
some other means bypassing io_nonblock()/io_block(), the result will be
stale.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
io_nonblock(3), io_block(3)
